  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 808 PM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nAs we start the following work week, the upper level pattern shows a\nlarge amplitude ridge over most of the central and eastern US. With\nhigh pressure situated underneath the ridge, expect hot and humid\nconditions to continue through the middle of next week. Afternoon\nhighs each afternoon will rise into the low to mid 90s with \novernight lows in the upper 60s to lower 70s. With dewpoints in the \nlower 70s, heat indices are forecast to top out between 98-104F. \nThis is just below Advisory criteria, but regardless NWS HeatRisk \nremains level 2 out of 4 (Moderate) through the end of the long term \nperiod. Outside of the heat, there is a low chance of an afternoon \nshower or thunderstorm Monday through Thursday.",
